<p>Opened in the early twentieth century opposite what is now the Prado Museum, the Palace was built in the same era of grand European hotels as the Ritz nearby, with wide corridors and a formal main entrance designed around carriage and, later, motor traffic. That history is part of why the departure experience here feels unhurried even in a busy capital city.</p>
